  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Skerry Light",
    "description": "A slim lighthouse on a skerry far out in the water, with no bridge and no beach: the only way there is by the rowing boat tied up under its ladder. Its lantern and window light up after dark in World View. 23 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Skerry** — two dark Block 2x2s make a low rock, 4 by 2, with Rocks round its foot and one on top. The south side is left clear for the boat.\n2. **Landing** — a Ladder up the rock's south face from the water, and a dark Half Cube on top for a bollard to tie up to.\n3. **Boat** — a blue Plate 2x4 hull turned 90° (press **R**), a Bench across it for the seat, and two Trims for oars, moored at the foot of the ladder.\n4. **Tower** — a Round Plate 2x2 on the rock, then two Pillars, white and red. The Door, turned 90°, faces the landing; a Small Window in the red band glows with lamplight at night.\n5. **Lantern** — a Round Plate 2x2, a Lantern that lights up after dark, another Round Plate 2x2 and a red Cone Roof.\n\nStand it out in open water, away from the shore, so the boat is the only way across.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Skerry: 2 Block 2x2, 6 Rock\n- Landing: 1 Ladder, 1 Half Cube\n- Boat: 1 Plate 2x4, 1 Bench, 2 Trim\n- Tower: 1 Round Plate 2x2, 2 Pillar, 1 Door, 1 Small Window\n- Lantern: 2 Round Plate 2x2, 1 Lantern, 1 Cone Roof\n\n23 bricks in all.\n",
